expected error that scales linearly with system size. Furthermore, we note that the
MM noncovalent pair interaction terms, which outnumber the covalent terms, are
more diﬃcult to assess with respect to their error contribution[85,86] because of their
distance and hence structure dependence. Regardless of the simpliﬁed assumptions inherent to Eq. (20) such as neglecting addi-
tional uncertainties introduced by the noncovalent interactions (see also Refs. [85,86]),
it is apparent that for large systems the energies of classical models may exhibit large
uncertainties (even with system-focused approaches). By contrast, atomic forces are
local quantities evaluated as partial ﬁrst-order derivatives at a given reference struc-
ture for each atomic nucleus. In view of these considerations, common practice in QM/MM studies is to gener-
ate and sample structures, either by molecular dynamics simulations or structure
optimizations."
4330,sample_en.pdf,sample_en.pdf-chunk-001,pdf,,1,425,/home/jose/repositories/kernel-boyacense/corpus_adl/data/sample_en.pdf,"We propose that during a molecular exploration, relevant structures should be iden-
tiﬁed with the complete QM/SFAM model (e.g., by molecular dynamics simulations
or structure optimizations), while for the energy diﬀerences of intermediate struc-
tures on the PES, the diﬀerence between the two strategies for computing the energy,
∆= ∆EQM/SFAM −∆Ered
