VII. QUESTION 7: APPLICATIONS OF MOORE MACHINES
Because Moore machines isolate their outputs from direct
combinational paths linked to inputs, they are favored in
systems requiring highly stable, synchronized signals [5]. Key
applications include:
1) Traffic Light Controllers: The state of the traffic light
purely dictates the output signals sent to the bulbs. Inputs
(like pedestrian buttons or car sensors) only influence
the next state transition, not the direct output, preventing
dangerous mid-cycle flickering. 2) Digital Counters and Clock Dividers: The output of
a digital counter is structurally identical to its current
state."
